CAT = "sgresPrivateSale"; SEG = "PVT"
Q = [
("A developer selling units in an uncompleted private housing project must hold:",
 "A housing developer's licence", ["A CEA estate agent licence", "An HDB sale permit", "A JTC allocation letter"],
 "Under the Housing Developers (Control and Licensing) Act 1965, a developer needs a licence from the Controller of Housing to sell units in a housing project."),
("For an uncompleted private home, the option to purchase and the sale and purchase agreement are:",
 "In prescribed standard forms", ["Freely drafted by developers", "Drafted by the buyer's agent", "Approved by CEA for each sale"],
 "The Housing Developers Rules prescribe the form of the option and the sale and purchase agreement, so key buyer protections cannot be drafted away."),
("Buyers of uncompleted private homes generally pay the price:",
 "By stages of construction", ["In full when the option is given", "Only on legal completion", "In monthly rent-like sums"],
 "Under the progressive payment scheme, instalments fall due as construction reaches set stages, such as the foundation, the roof and TOP."),
("After vacant possession of a new private home, the developer must make good defects reported within:",
 "The defects liability period", ["The option period", "The minimum occupation period", "The cooling-off period"],
 "The standard sale and purchase agreement gives a defects liability period, 12 months from vacant possession, during which the developer must rectify defects at its cost."),
("Under caveat emptor, a buyer of a completed private home is expected to:",
 "Inspect and check it himself", ["Rely on the seller to list faults", "Expect free repairs after sale", "Leave all checks to the agent"],
 "Let the buyer beware: the seller need not point out patent physical defects, so the buyer should inspect and investigate. The seller must still not misrepresent or conceal."),
("Legal requisitions sent to government agencies during a sale mainly check whether the property:",
 "Is affected by public schemes", ["Suits the buyer's budget", "Has a registered agent", "Was originally bought with CPF savings"],
 "Requisitions to bodies such as LTA, URA and PUB reveal road lines, drainage reserves, acquisition plans or unauthorised works that may affect the property."),
("Lawyers run a bankruptcy search against the seller during a sale mainly because:",
 "A bankrupt cannot pass good title", ["It shows the seller's credit score", "It fixes the stamp duty payable", "It confirms the CPF to refund"],
 "A bankrupt's property vests in the Official Assignee, so a bankrupt seller cannot complete the sale. The search protects the buyer before completion."),
("Under the Law Society's Conditions of Sale, the balance of the price on completion is paid to:",
 "A solicitor's conveyancing account", ["The seller's salesperson in cash", "The buyer's salesperson to hold", "The seller's personal bank account"],
 "Conveyancing money is paid into the conveyancing account of the seller's solicitor, which protects both sides and keeps salespersons away from transaction monies."),
("If the seller fails to pay seller's stamp duty that is due, the Conditions of Sale let the buyer:",
 "Deduct it from the price", ["Cancel the purchase at once", "Charge it to the salesperson", "Ignore it entirely"],
 "Because IRAS can recover unpaid SSD, the Conditions of Sale allow the buyer to deduct the SSD charged from the purchase price and pay it."),
("In a condominium, the common property is managed and maintained by:",
 "The management corporation", ["Each subsidiary proprietor", "The developer forever", "URA's estate office"],
 "Under the Building Maintenance and Strata Management Act 2004, the MCST manages common property, enforces by-laws and collects contributions from subsidiary proprietors."),
("Strata owners' contributions to the sinking fund pay for:",
 "Long-term repairs and renewal", ["Daily cleaning and security guards", "The developer's profit", "Each owner's property tax"],
 "The sinking fund builds reserves for major future work, such as repainting or replacing lifts. Day-to-day costs come from the management fund."),
("For a collective sale of a development that is 10 or more years old, consent is needed from owners of at least:",
 "80% of share value and area", ["90% of share value and area", "50% of share value only", "Every owner without exception"],
 "Under the Land Titles (Strata) Act, developments 10 years or older need 80% of share values and total strata area; younger ones need 90%."),
("If minority owners object to a collective sale that reached the consent level, the application is decided by:",
 "The Strata Titles Boards", ["CEA's disciplinary panel", "URA's planning department", "The MCST council"],
 "The Strata Titles Boards hear collective sale applications and objections, and their orders can be taken to the High Court."),
("Before renting a private home to a foreign tenant, the landlord's salesperson should check that the tenant:",
 "Holds a valid immigration pass", ["Has a home address abroad", "Can show a recent payslip from work", "Owns a credit card"],
 "Under the Immigration Act, renting to someone without a valid pass, such as an overstayer, is an offence. CEA's guidelines require checking the tenant's identity and pass."),
("URA requires private homes to be rented out for a minimum stay of:",
 "Three consecutive months", ["One consecutive week", "One calendar month", "Six consecutive months"],
 "URA does not allow short-term rentals of private homes, such as daily or weekly stays; each occupant must stay at least three consecutive months."),
("Letting premises knowing they will be used as a brothel is an offence under:",
 "The Women's Charter", ["The PDPA", "The Consumer Protection Act", "The Land Titles Act"],
 "The Women's Charter makes it an offence to let premises knowing they will be used for prostitution, which is why landlords and salespersons must vet tenants."),
]
